# Work tracking (GitHub)

This repo uses **GitHub** ([Unthred/BuildMonitor](https://github.com/Unthred/BuildMonitor)) — Issues and `gh` CLI, not Azure DevOps.

## Conventions

- **Features and enhancements:** GitHub **Issue** with a clear title.
- **Defects:** Issue with prefix `Bug:` when helpful.
- **Branches:** `feature/<id>-short-kebab-name` (example: `feature/42-live-build-log`).
- **Pull requests:** body must include `Closes #<id>` (see [.github/pull_request_template.md](../../.github/pull_request_template.md)).
- **Commits:** prefix with `#<id>:` when an issue applies (example: `#42: Debounce run log saves`).

## Issue policy (moderate)

| Change type | Issue required? |
|-------------|-----------------|
| Feature, bug fix, behaviour change | **Yes** — create or link existing issue |
| Docs/rules-only chore | **No** — if user says `docs only`, `rules only`, or `no issue` |
| Tiny typo / comment | **No** — unless user wants tracking |

Before `git commit` or **ship it** on feature work without a supplied issue number:

1. Use a supplied id — `#42`, “for issue 42”, or branch `feature/42-...`.
2. Resolve one (in order): branch name → conversation + files changed → `gh issue list`.
3. If exactly one plausible issue — tell the user which you chose, then commit.
4. If several fit or none fit — **ask** or offer `gh issue create`.
5. Do not push feature work directly to `main` without user explicitly requesting a hotfix.

**Exception:** user explicitly says “no issue”, “chore only”, or “docs/rules only”.

## Agent automation (`gh`)

```powershell
gh issue create --title "..." --body "..."
gh issue view 42
gh issue list --state open
gh pr create --title "#42: ..." --body "Closes #42`n`n..."
gh pr merge <n> --squash
```

Details: [docs/ops/github-workflow.md](../../docs/ops/github-workflow.md).

## “Ship it” (agent)

When the user says **ship** or **ship it**, follow **`feature-ship`** skill:

1. Commit + push on `feature/<id>-...`
2. Create PR if none (`Closes #<id>` in body)
3. **Merge** the PR into `main` (when user asked for full ship)

**Ready for review** / **open PR** → commit + push + active PR only; do not merge unless asked.

## Record of intent

Chat and Cursor plan files are not the system of record. **GitHub Issues** plus **PR descriptions** plus **`docs/`** are.
